## Configure OpenHPC on the Compute Nodes

Apply the baseline compute-node configuration: disable the firewall, point
chrony at the head node, add the NFS client mounts, and enable the cluster
services. The service enables come last -- a stateful node runs this
configuration after boot with no further restart, so the settings must be in
place before the services start. The scheduler's own configuration follows in
the next section.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Configure OpenHPC on the compute nodes -->
```bash
# Disable the firewall on the compute nodes
{{ compute_service_disable("firewalld.service") }}

# Point time synchronization at the head node
{{ compute_run("echo server ${sms_ip} iburst >> /etc/chrony.conf") }}

# NFS client mounts of /home and the OpenHPC public tree
{{ compute_run("echo ${sms_ip}:/home /home nfs nfsvers=4,nodev,nosuid >> /etc/fstab") }}
{{ compute_run("echo ${sms_ip}:/opt/ohpc/pub /opt/ohpc/pub nfs nfsvers=4,nodev >> /etc/fstab") }}
{%- if is_xcat_stateful %}
{{ compute_run("mkdir -p /opt/ohpc/pub") }}
{{ compute_run("mount -a") }}
{%- endif %}

# Enable the cluster services
{{ compute_service_enable("munge.service") }}
{{ compute_service_enable("chronyd.service") }}
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->
